{"builder":"Make one pull request that adds a --shout flag to greet-cli and meets every line of issue #12's expect list.\n\nContext: bin/greet.js picks the first argument that does not start with `--` as the name and prints `${greeting(name)}\\n` (greeting is in src/greet.js and returns `Hello, <name>!`). docs/index.md is the usage page. .github/workflows/pages.yml publishes the docs/ directory to GitHub Pages on push to main. Tests use `node --test` (test/greet.test.js).\n\nSteps:\n1. In bin/greet.js, detect `--shout` in process.argv.slice(2). When it is present, print the greeting converted to upper case (for example `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` prints `HELLO, ADA!` followed by a newline). The flag must work whether it comes before or after the name. When `--shout` is absent, the output must stay byte-for-byte the same as now (`Hello, Ada!\\n` for `Ada`). The usage error and exit code 2 for a missing name stay the same.\n2. Leave the `greeting` export in src/greet.js unchanged in behaviour. If you add a helper, keep the existing test passing.\n3. Add tests to test/greet.test.js: `--shout Ada` gives `HELLO, ADA!\\n`, `Ada --shout` gives the same, and plain `Ada` still gives `Hello, Ada!\\n`.\n4. Update docs/index.md to document `--shout`: show the usage line `node bin/greet.js --shout <name>` and say that it prints the greeting in upper case. Keep the existing plain usage. Do not move the docs out of docs/ and do not change .github/workflows/pages.yml: that workflow publishes docs/ to https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ after merge, which is how the last expect line gets met.\n5. Run `npm test` and make sure it passes. Also run `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` and `node bin/greet.js Ada` by hand to confirm the outputs.\n6. Open the pull request. Put a link to https://github.com/o/greet-cli/issues/12 in the description, and note that the published docs page updates only after merge, through the pages workflow.","verifier":"Check the pull request at its head against issue #12's expect lines, one check per line, in order. Check out the PR head and run everything from the repository root.\n\nCheck 1. Expect line: \"node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\"\nRun: `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` and `node bin/greet.js --shout 'Grace Hopper'`. For reference, also run `node -e \"import('./src/greet.js').then(m=>console.log(m.greeting('Ada')))\"` to get the normal greeting.\nPASS: each command exits 0 and its stdout is the normal greeting for that name in upper case (for Ada: `HELLO, ADA!`).\nFAIL: a non-zero exit, output that is not upper case, output that differs from the upper-cased greeting, or `--shout` printed as the name.\n\nCheck 2. Expect line: \"without --shout the output is unchanged\"\nRun: `node bin/greet.js Ada` and `node bin/greet.js 'Grace Hopper'` at the PR head. Then run the same commands at the merge base (`git merge-base HEAD origin/HEAD`, or the base commit of the PR) in a separate checkout or worktree, and compare. Also run `npm test` at the head.\nPASS: the stdout and exit code at the head are byte-for-byte the same as at the base (`Hello, Ada!\\n` for Ada).\nFAIL: any difference in stdout or exit code without --shout.\n\nCheck 3. Expect line: \"docs/index.md documents --shout\"\nRead docs/index.md at the PR head.\nPASS: the file mentions `--shout` and says what it does, i.e. that it prints the greeting in upper case.\nFAIL: `--shout` is not mentioned, or its effect is not described.\n\nCheck 4. Expect line: \"after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\"\nThis can only be seen after merge. Do not fetch or read the live page. Instead, check what the head contains that will produce it: read .github/workflows/pages.yml at the head and confirm that it still runs on push to main and uploads the `docs` directory as the Pages artifact (actions/upload-pages-artifact with path docs, then actions/deploy-pages). Then confirm that docs/index.md at the head contains `--shout` (run `grep -n -- --shout docs/index.md`).\nPASS: the workflow publishes docs/ on push to main and docs/index.md at the head lists --shout, so the published page will list --shout once the PR is merged. In the report, say that the live result can only be seen after merge.\nFAIL: the workflow no longer publishes docs/ on push to main, or docs/index.md at the head does not contain --shout.\n\nAdvisory (does not affect PASS or FAIL):\n- Check that `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` (flag after the name) also shouts.\n- Check that `node bin/greet.js --shout` with no name still prints the usage error and exits 2.\n- Check that new tests in test/greet.test.js cover both the --shout and the plain output, and that `npm test` passes."}